\title{Smart Contract Vulnerabilities Due to Poor Specification}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2025-09-06}
\meta{toc}{true}

\p{
    Smart contracts are vulnerable due to incorrect code, but equally due to incorrect specification
    (or design). There are more examples of this that can possibly be included here, but I have
    written up a few examples. We would recognize each of these exploits as attacks, despite the
    fact that the contracts were functioning as specified, which tells us that the specifications
    were erroneous as they did not accurately capture the intended economic behaviors. To the
    contrary, they permitted unintended and pathological behavior.
}

